# The manifests are DATA, parsed field-by-field on three platforms — never source to be
# normalised to the checkout's native line ending. Under a CRLF checkout the trailing \r
# lands on each row's LAST field, which on a three-column row is the class name, so the
# class lookup missed and those rows scored a vacuous pass. Pinning LF fixes it at the
# source; the parsers strip \r as well, because a manifest can also arrive from outside
# this checkout.
*.tsv text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
